{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgiCVeCC68ohMPoFd3zqc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01R4Yk1VThYHWKzfrJdnbRKN","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"$WSROOT/laya/s0/fable-high-code-r2/step2/NOTES.md","content":"# Step 2 notes: card PIN -> cards\n\n## Rule added\nA message that contains the word \"PIN\" (or \"pins\") is routed to `cards`.\nThis covers changing, resetting, unblocking a PIN, wrong PIN tries, and an\naccount locked by PIN tries. It fires on any Laya answer, so the one evidence\nrow Laya sent to `disputes` is fixed too.\n\n## Boundaries kept\n- \"passcode\" is not matched. The app passcode stays with `account_security`.\n- An unrecognised or unauthorised transaction that mentions a PIN stays a\n  dispute (\"someone used my card and PIN, I don't recognise this\").\n- Correction 1 (bad exchange rate -> `fees_fx`) runs first and is unchanged.\n- The ATM cost rule from step 1 is unchanged.\n\n## Order in `route`\n1. Exchange-rate complaint -> `fees_fx`\n2. PIN query -> `cards`\n3. ATM cost with Laya = cards -> `fees_fx`\n4. Otherwise Laya's answer\n\n## Check\nRan all 32 evidence rows plus 9 guard cases (earlier correction, passcode,\nidentity, close account, dispute with PIN) with the lab venv Python.\nResult: 32/32 evidence, 9/9 guards.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":436,"cache_read_input_tokens":66569,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":436},"output_tokens":48,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f6f0c811-fa84-486e-a3d5-34d547807295","uuid":"af8e889b-654d-457e-9d65-697f1f386b47","timestamp":"2026-11-04T16:25:06.476Z","request_id":"req_011CgiCVdsbPVYbib8A